<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47633" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσύ̆χ-ιος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁσ-</span></b>  (v.l.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσ-</span></b> ), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥσυχος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>still, quiet, at rest</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσύχιον δ᾽ ἄρα μιν πολέμου ἔκπεμπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.598
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρήνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					9.22
				</span></i>
			; also in Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόπον ἡ</span>.
			of a <i>quiet</i> disposition, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.107
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἡ. ὁ σώφρων βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Chrm.</u>
					160b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἡ. πράξεις</span> ib. c; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἡ. ἦθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					604e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἡ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				3.2.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἡ. τῆς εἰρήνης</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥσυχον</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.120
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>
			<i>more reposeful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.60S.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					438
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				179e
			</span></i>.</div>
